	(footprint "_mech:RCA105"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "c144853f-7570-485b-81b7-b8654642524b")
		(at 100.2 122)
		(descr "RCA (phono) jack RCA-105, right-angle PCB mount, hand-soldered (not JLC-assembled). Land pattern per the manufacturer drawing \"RCA-105 / T:1.6 Dimensions of PC board holes, tolerance +-0.1 (Printed-bottom view)\": TWO slots, both on the connector axis: pad1 2.30x1.50 at 4.80 behind the reference plane, pad2 1.00x2.30 at 8.30 behind the reference plane. pad1 = shell/GND, pad2 = centre conductor (signal). Both pads sit on the axis, so the bottom-view drawing needs no mirroring. Origin = reference plane (x=0, put the board edge here) on the barrel axis (y=0). Frame 10.00 wide x 13.00 high, body 10.00+-0.20 deep behind the reference plane; barrel phi8.30+-0.10 protrudes 9.30 IN FRONT of the reference plane (overhangs the board edge); barrel axis sits 8.00 above the PCB surface (5.00 below the top of the frame); legs 3.70 long.")
		(tags "rca phono jack RCA-105 right-angle")
